1
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:30,880
You big dummy.

2
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,520
Assaulting a police officer?

3
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,160
Still want to fight?

4
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,020
I was wrong. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

5
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,800
Look at you.

6
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,460
You've gotten a lot stronger.

7
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,680
I heard you went from a small director

8
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,240
to a big one.

9
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:47,920
What do you think?

10
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,160
Do you think I'll

11
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:50,680
become a famous director first,

12
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,160
or you'll become the police captain first?

13
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,400
I'm working hard too.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,440
Can't we do it at the same time?

15
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:56,640
You don't deserve it.

16
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:59,000
I do.

17
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:00,720
Let's eat.

18
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:01,840
How about this place?

19
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:02,770
This one is fine.

20
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:03,880
You're so tall.

21
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:04,800
Duck a little.

22
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,000
Li Xingchen,

23
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,000
Li Xingchen.

24
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:31,280
I have nothing left.

25
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,960
Are you sure you want to leave me?

26
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:39,650
I don't deserve to be a detective anymore.

27
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,000
Because of this,

28
00:01:47,039 --> 00:01:48,640
we can't be friends anymore.

29
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,720
Take care.

30
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,680
Take care.

31
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:29,520
I'm sorry.

32
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,120
I'm sorry.

33
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:53,079
Pull over.

34
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,280
Go.

35
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,120
Do you even know how to drive?

36
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,240
What did I do, officer?

37
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,760
Did you yield to the pedestrian just now?

38
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,440
Driver's license and vehicle registration.

39
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,160
I'm sorry,

40
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:06,880
officer.

41
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,180
I was in a bit of a hurry.

42
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,160
I don't think it's a big deal.

43
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,640
Please cut me

44
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:12,480
some slack.

45
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,160
I'll definitely be more careful next time.

46
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,600
I'll give you a pass this time.

47
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,760
Thank you, officer.

48
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:17,360
Off you go.

49
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,900
License plate C 73194.

50
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,120
This isn't right.

51
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:36,640
That traffic cop's uniform looks off, too.

52
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:38,320
And his hand signals

53
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,120
are wrong.

54
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,440
Hello, 110?

55
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:44,420
I want to make a report.

56
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:49,440
Hello.

57
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:50,440
Hello, ma'am.

58
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:51,840
I'm a police officer.

59
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,320
Can I ask you something?

60
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,000
Go ahead.

61
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,280
Is this tricycle yours?

62
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,360
No, it's not.

63
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:58,360
Not yours.

64
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,360
Do you know whose it is then?

65
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,960
I don't know.

66
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,240
Why are you asking?

67
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,360
Well,

68
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,160
this tricycle is blocking the road.

69
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,000
We have to take it back to our unit first.

70
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,120
I need to know whose it is

71
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,040
so I can return it,

72
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:10,520
right?

73
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:12,320
So you don't know?

74
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:13,320
I don't know.

75
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,360
This piece of junk

76
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,760
was probably abandoned.

77
00:04:16,519 --> 00:04:17,250
Understood.

78
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,490
Thanks. That's all.

79
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,000
Okay.

80
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:19,920
Ping Fu'an.

81
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,560
Hello.

82
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,280
Have you seen this vehicle?

83
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,880
No, I haven't.

84
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:24,920
Okay. Thank you.

85
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,620
Never seen him.

86
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:28,560
Have you seen him?

87
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,620
Never seen him. No.

88
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,480
Okay, thanks.

89
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:34,520
Any luck?

90
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:37,600
Everyone here

91
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,730
says they haven't seen him.

92
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:40,640
Yeah.

93
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:41,440
That's weird.

94
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,120
They all denied seeing him.

95
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,780
None of them have seen him.

96
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:45,960
Something's definitely wrong.

97
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,200
That's a breakthrough.

98
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,600
It's worth looking into.

99
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:50,560
Hello?

100
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,020
Captain Li,

101
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:55,240
someone reported a fake traffic cop.

102
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:55,840
Copy that.

103
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,360
Let's go.

104
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,020
Do you see that guy?

105
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:26,890
He's gonna run as soon as he sees us.

106
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,440
Stay close on the bike.

107
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:28,880
Got it.

108
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:29,280
POLICE

109
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,120
Captain Li,

110
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,600
there's something wrong with those two.

111
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,860
See the one next to him?

112
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:38,000
Jiang, get the car ready.

113
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,480
Si, looks like the real police are here.

114
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:45,800
Should we run?

115
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:31,480
Freeze!

116
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,880
Take off your masks

117
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:41,800
and helmets.

118
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:49,840
That's right.

119
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,840
Just do as you're told.

120
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:54,880
Captain Li,

121
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,400
let's take them

122
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:57,770
back to the station.

123
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,320
Don't move.

124
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,160
Don't move.

125
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:12,480
Get up.

126
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:13,210
Let's go.

127
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,000
Oh my god.

128
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,360
It's bleeding.

129
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,080
Kid,

130
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,560
have some water.

131
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,400
You must be tired
after running for so long.

132
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,330
What are you looking at?

133
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,040
You think you're justified?

134
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:33,920
Look at you.

135
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,040
A big boy,

136
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,840
yet you bite people like a puppy.

137
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:39,880
Tell me.

138
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,000
Name.

139
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,200
Si.

140
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,159
Full name.

141
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,040
Bai Xiaosi.

142
00:07:46,440 --> 00:07:46,880
The real name on your ID card. 045509.

143
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,080
The real name on your ID card.

144
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,210
That is my real name.

145
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:49,680
Bai.

146
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:51,600
ID number.

147
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,920
045509. You're only 17.

148
00:07:57,920 --> 00:07:59,580
045509, you're still a minor.

149
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,210
My birthday is in a few days.

150
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,120
Besides,

151
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,900
you don't look much older than me. You...

152
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,720
17 years old.

153
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:10,040
You must be in school. Which one?

154
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,200
I dropped out a long time ago.

155
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,680
Take a look at this guy.

156
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,010
Is he the fake traffic cop
from that night?

157
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,980
Doesn't look like him.

158
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:29,740
Doesn't look like him,

159
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,720
or isn't him?

160
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,320
I can't be sure.

161
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,360
That night,

162
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,720
the man was wearing a mask.

163
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:46,160
Jiang,

164
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,960
put a mask on him.

165
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,420
Copy that, Captain Li.

166
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,090
Look over there.

167
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,040
Look here.

168
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,920
I'm sure.

169
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,200
It's not him.

170
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:02,920
You're that sure?

171
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:06,840
That man's eyes

172
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,680
slanted upwards,

173
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,600
kind of like phoenix eyes.

174
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,640
And

175
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,900
his eyelashes were very long.

176
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,620
You remember it that clearly?

177
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,840
Because only his eyes
were showing at the time.

178
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,440
I remember

179
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,170
there were raindrops clinging

180
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:26,680
to his eyelashes.

181
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:31,840
Got it.

182
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:33,040
Where were you between 7:00 and 8:00 p.m.

183
00:09:33,040 --> 00:09:34,240
on October 23rd?

184
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:36,640
At a bar.

185
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,560
Which bar?

186
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,040
Du World,

187
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,760
the one at the west gate
of the Second Factory.

188
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,920
Can anyone prove it?

189
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,040
Of course.

190
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,480
It was my girlfriend's birthday
that night,

191
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,120
and several of her besties were there.

192
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,520
You have a girlfriend at 17?

193
00:09:49,320 --> 00:09:50,560
What's wrong, officer?

194
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:51,640
It's not illegal, is it?

195
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:52,440
It's not.

196
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:55,850
Give me your girlfriend's name
and phone number.

197
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,360
Bai Xiaosi.

198
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:02,360
Where did you get this uniform?

199
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,620
Why are you impersonating a traffic cop?

200
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,920
Bai Xiaosi, right?

201
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,760
Let me tell you,

202
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,160
we strongly suspect

203
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:14,020
you're involved in a murder case.

204
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,120
If you really didn't do it,

205
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,640
come clean

206
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:20,480
and tell us everything you know.

207
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:22,760
Don't get yourself implicated, got it?

208
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,600
M-Murder?

209
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,560
I didn't do it.

210
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:26,720
I didn't do anything.

211
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:27,360
I-I just

212
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,680
impersonated a traffic cop
and shot some videos.

213
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,680
Tell the truth.

214
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,880
What was your motive?

215
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:35,080
It was just cosplay.

216
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:35,840
Bai Xiaosi,

217
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,420
you're really something.

218
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:38,800
You dressed up as a cop

219
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,600
and dared to direct traffic on the street.

220
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:41,930
Are you that shameless?

221
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,260
I've admired the police since I was a kid.

222
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,360
I feel so cool in a police uniform.

223
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,000
Then one time,

224
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,760
I went to a school gate to direct traffic,

225
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:50,680
just for kicks,

226
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:53,040
so I had my girlfriend record it

227
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,100
and post it online.

228
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,000
Hello,

229
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,520
Wenwen.

230
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,160
Did you see our video?

231
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:15,240
It went viral.

232
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,840
The view count is super high.

233
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:18,570
And there are so many comments.

234
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,000
I have to say, this trick really worked.

235
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:22,880
Is that it?

236
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:24,760
That's it.

237
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,040
Just so

238
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:27,440
the video could go viral?

239
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:30,360
Do you know how hard it is, officer?

240
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,000
If this post goes viral,

241
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,200
I'll become famous.

242
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,400
I'll have my own fans.

243
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,060
Do you guys know what fans are?

244
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:37,660
Captain Li,

245
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,820
we've been waiting

246
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:39,760
for you.

247
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:40,880
Come on.

248
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:41,480
Have a seat.

249
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,280
Sorry

250
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,200
for keeping you all waiting.

251
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,800
I'll drink three glasses
as an apology later, okay?

252
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:45,400
No need.

253
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,520
You're a captain now.

254
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:47,520
We understand you're busy.

255
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,400
Right, guys?

256
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,800
Deputy.

257
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:52,280
Just keeping busy.

258
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,040
Sit.

259
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,000
Alright, come on.

260
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:56,880
Classmates,

261
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:57,840
with Li Xingchen here,

262
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:59,040
everyone's present.

263
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,240
Come on, let's raise our glasses.

264
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:02,100
May our friendship last forever.

265
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,480
To our friendship.

266
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,240
Captain Li, stop looking.

267
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,570
Song Yanfei isn't here.

268
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:15,480
Xingchen,

269
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:16,880
you two were so close.

270
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:19,410
Hasn't he contacted you
these past few years?

271
00:13:19,680 --> 00:13:20,160
No.

272
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:21,700
Come on,

273
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:22,960
for our second glass,

274
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,120
I wish all of us

275
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,200
more wealth,

276
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,240
better health,

277
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:27,640
and happier families.

278
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:28,570
Come on, cheers!

279
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,600
Alright, cheers!

280
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,280
Let's eat.

281
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:39,020
Come on.

282
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:58,440
Captain Li,

283
00:13:59,080 --> 00:13:59,680
how is it?

284
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,480
Perfect timing, right?

285
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,570
Why are you here?

286
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,440
I figured you couldn't drive

287
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:05,840
after drinking,

288
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:06,960
so I went out to buy some stuff

289
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,200
and dropped by

290
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,560
to be your driver.

291
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,290
Is this your car?

292
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:12,760
Yours?

293
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,720
My dad's is mine.

294
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,360
Get in.

295
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:28,040
I heard

296
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:29,810
Song Yanfei is back in our city.

297
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,120
Who told you? Is it true?

298
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:34,760
It's true.

299
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,240
My wife saw him

300
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:38,760
at the Cultural Palace a few days ago.

301
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:40,080
But strangely,

302
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:42,040
when she said hi,

303
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,240
he ignored her.

304
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,720
Maybe he didn't hear her.

305
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:47,920
Alright,

306
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:48,800
I'm leaving.

307
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:49,400
Bye.

308
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,560
I heard you're back.

309
00:15:05,480 --> 00:15:06,940
Aren't you going to say hi?

310
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:14,200
Captain

311
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:16,560
Li,

312
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:19,760
What is it?

313
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:21,280
I found Li Fang,

314
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,160
the organizer of

315
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:23,760
the dance competition.

316
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,690
Let's go see him.

317
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:27,720
That was fast.

318
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:28,560
Good job.

319
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:32,980
Captain Li,

320
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,160
are you

321
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:34,960
upset

322
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:35,960
about the

323
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:37,040
class reunion?

324
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,200
Was your first love not there,

325
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,400
or was she there

326
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,060
but you're not her fiancé?

327
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:46,360
Keep running your mouth.

328
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:47,920
By the way,

329
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,080
we need to see Gao Yayan tomorrow.

330
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,040
Go inform Wei.

331
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,000
Okay, okay.

332
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,040
Let's go.

333
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,840
I used to come to this cultural palace

334
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:10,760
when I was a kid.

335
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,220
It's still the same river.

336
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,400
Gao Yayan called me

337
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,800
and asked if it was okay to meet here.

338
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:18,160
I asked why.

339
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:21,240
She said she was accompanying
her boyfriend for a rehearsal here.

340
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:22,840
Rehearsal? What rehearsal?

341
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:23,770
I don't know.

342
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,520
Seems like a dance drama.

343
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,560
According to Gao Yayan,

344
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,560
her boyfriend seems to be an artist.

345
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,640
Something's wrong.

346
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:33,880
Gao Yayan

347
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,080
wasn't sad at all when her father

348
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,340
passed away last time.

349
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:38,880
And now she's in the mood to accompany
her boyfriend for a rehearsal.

350
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:39,640
Exactly.

351
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:40,800
When Wei asked her that day,

352
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:41,920
she overreacted.

353
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,530
I think Gao Yayan still has some clues.

354
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,320
Let's go. Let's go in.

355
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:01,120
Wait.

356
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,440
Why do I feel like I've seen
a dance drama with this theme

357
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:07,000
somewhere?

358
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,560
Officers, please come in.

359
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:21,920
Five, six, seven, go.

360
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:25,800
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

361
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:28,560
Two, two, three, four, five, six.

362
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:29,960
Xiaoyu,

363
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,640
formation. Move in.

364
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,080
Right, remember it.

365
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:34,080
Let's do it again.

366
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,760
This is my boyfriend.

367
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:39,000
He's rehearsing a dance drama

368
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,000
called "Circle".

369
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:41,680
It's roughly about...

370
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,080
We all live in

371
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:44,360
different circles.

372
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:45,280
So we explore

373
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:47,280
whether this is the life
we chose for ourselves,

374
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:48,000
or if

375
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,120
we are actually living in

376
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,800
a circle drawn by others.

377
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,240
Okay.

378
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:53,120
Much better than the past two days.

379
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,280
And tomorrow, same time, same place.

380
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:56,000
All right.

381
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,880
Dismissed. Good work, everyone.

382
00:17:58,880 --> 00:17:59,680
Good work.

383
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,960
Put your coats on. Put your coats on.
Put your coats on.

384
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,680
Is your dad picking you up today too?

385
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,940
Go on. Go find your dad.

386
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,320
Hurry up and put your coat on.

